# Case-study TRE specs — parametric request/grant arbiter
# phi_k: every r gets a g response within [0,k] time,
#         only idle events (a) allowed between r and g.
# Outer [0,100] bound makes volume finite and T auto-sampleable.
#
# Existing specs for reference:
#   phi_1 (unbounded r->g):  spec_02_subset_A.tre
#   phi_2 (r->g in [1,2]):   spec_02_subset_B.tre

### phi_k5: response within [0,5]
<(a + g)*. (<r . (a)*. g>_[0,5]. (a + g)*)* >_[0,100]

### phi_k10: response within [0,10]
# <(a + g)*. (<r . (a)*. g>_[0,10]. (a + g)*)* >_[0,100]

### phi_k15: response within [0,15]
# <(a + g)*. (<r . (a)*. g>_[0,15]. (a + g)*)* >_[0,100]
